\"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1286, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:57\", \"token_count\": 609, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Opt-Out Behaviour Designed\\n\\nThe CLI and API collect anonymous usage metrics (pages processed, OCR fallback rate) to help tune the detection engine. Setting `CIPHER_TELEMETRY=0`, or the equivalent GUI toggle, is designed to immediately stop all outbound telemetry traffic to the metrics endpoint.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Design-Time Issue Found and Patched: Pending-Queue Leak\\n\\nWhile designing the flag semantics, testing surfaced that the opt-out flag blocked network egress correctly, but the `TelemetryLogger` kept writing event payloads to a local SQLite queue regardless. That meant re-enabling telemetry later would flush the entire backlog accumulated during the opt-out period, including events the user believed were never being recorded. The logger was patched to a no-op backend when opted out, closing that gap before the flag semantics were finalized.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Verification (Retrospective)\\n\\nA network trace on 2026-08-24 confirmed zero outbound telemetry traffic once the opt-out flag is set, closing the CLI-side verification as Completed.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Remaining Limitation\\n\\nThe third-party Electron crash reporter (Sentry) has not been audited for whether it independently respects the opt-out environment variable or requires its own disable hook for minidump uploads.\\n\\n*Note*: CLI-side telemetry opt-out is verified. Full privacy compliance for air-gapped/opt-out users cannot be claimed until the Sentry crash-reporter path is audited separately.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 opt out behaviour design the cli and api collect anonym usag metric page process ocr fallback rate to help tune the detect engin set cipher _ telemetri 0 or the equival gui toggl is design to immedi stop all outbound telemetri traffic to the metric endpoint sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 design time issu found and patch pend queue leak while design the flag semant test surfac that the opt out flag block network egress correct but the telemetrylogg kept write event payload to a local sqlite queue regardless that meant re enabl telemetri later would flush the entir backlog accumul dure the opt out period includ event the user believ were never be record the logger wa patch to a no op backend when opt out close that gap befor the flag semant were final sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 verif retrospect a network trace on 2026 08 24 confirm zero outbound telemetri traffic onc the opt out flag is set close the cli side verif a complet sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 remain limit the third parti electron crash report sentri ha not been audit for whether it independ respect the opt out environ variabl or requir it own disabl hook for minidump upload note cli side telemetri opt out is verifi full privaci complianc for air gap opt out user can not be claim until the sentri crash report path is audit separ\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9e43bb08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"id\": \"c3381a6a564a6c9c\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3099778051178006, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12263576588257229, \"vector_similarity\": 0.74710923, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9e43bb08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1587, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:00:54\", \"token_count\": 503, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-24\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Title**: Manual Review Threshold for Low-Confidence OCR\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-25\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nBuild manual-review quarantine logic for low-confidence OCR output (WS-04). Diana implemented threshold logic, a quarantine folder for low-confidence pages, and quarantine metadata (confidence, page, reason); Charlie added visual UI indicators for quarantined pages. An end-to-end quarantine test exercised the UI and metadata path, but the 90% confidence-threshold integration is still in progress and the task remains Active.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-24\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Title**: Manual Review Threshold for Low-Confidence OCR\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-25\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Quarantine folder, metadata, and UI indicators integrate end-to-end (exercised, not yet fully done).\\n\\n- 90% confidence-threshold logic fully integrated with the quarantine path (still in progress; task remains Active).\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-24\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Title**: Manual Review Threshold for Low-Confidence OCR\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-25\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nBuild manual-review quarantine logic for low-confidence OCR output (WS-04). Diana implemented threshold logic, a quarantine folder for low-confidence pages, and quarantine metadata (confidence, page, reason); Charlie added visual UI indicators for quarantined pages. An end-to-end quarantine test exercised the UI and metadata path, but the 90% confidence-threshold integration is still in progress and the task remains Active.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-24\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Title**: Manual Review Threshold for Low-Confidence OCR\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-25\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-06-25**: Diana - Task Create (Open)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 24 sourc id src cu ciph 24 task id ciph 24 titl manual review threshold for low confid ocr status activ assigne diana prioriti normal date creat 2026 06 25 descript build m