{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37"],"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]},"page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false,"question":"OCR confidence below 90 worker crash batch abort manual review quarantine not applied fail closed policy precedence"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \" - *Task opened to design the manual-review quarantine workflow for low-confidence OCR.*\\n\\n- **2026-09-18**: Diana - End-to-end quarantine test; 90% threshold still integrating (Active)\\n\\n - *Ran an end-to-end quarantine test exercising the UI and metadata path; confidence-threshold integration remains Active.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"task open to design the manual review quarantin workflow for low confid ocr 2026 09 18 diana end to end quarantin test 90 threshold still integr activ ran an end to end quarantin test exercis the ui and metadata path confid threshold integr remain activ\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e959cb748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"id\": \"e90e536e6f3595fa\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.31312695827068204, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10614438324383148, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7960863, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e959cb748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1286, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:57\", \"token_count\": 609, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-24\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Title**: Manual Review Threshold for Low-Confidence OCR\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-25\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nBuild manual-review quarantine logic for low-confidence OCR output (WS-04). Diana implemented threshold logic, a quarantine folder for low-confidence pages, and quarantine metadata (confidence, page, reason); Charlie added visual UI indicators for quarantined pages. An end-to-end quarantine test exercised the UI and metadata path, but the 90% confidence-threshold integration is still in progress and the task remains Active.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-24\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Title**: Manual Review Threshold for Low-Confidence OCR\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-25\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Quarantine folder, metadata, and UI indicators integrate end-to-end (exercised, not yet fully done).\\n\\n- 90% confidence-threshold logic fully integrated with the quarantine path (still in progress; task remains Active).\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-24\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Title**: Manual Review Threshold for Low-Confidence OCR\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-25\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nBuild manual-review quarantine logic for low-confidence OCR output (WS-04). Diana implemented threshold logic, a quarantine folder for low-confidence pages, and quarantine metadata (confidence, page, reason); Charlie added visual UI indicators for quarantined pages. An end-to-end quarantine test exercised the UI and metadata path, but the 90% confidence-threshold integration is still in progress and the task remains Active.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-24\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Title**: Manual Review Threshold for Low-Confidence OCR\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-25\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-06-25**: Diana - Task Create (Open)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 24 sourc id src cu ciph 24 task id ciph 24 titl manual review threshold for low confid ocr status activ assigne diana prioriti normal date creat 2026 06 25 descript build manual review quarantin logic for low confid ocr output w 04 diana implement threshold logic a quarantin folder for low confid page and quarantin metadata confid page reason charli ad visual ui indic for quarantin page an end to end quarantin test exercis the ui and metadata path but the 90 confid threshold integr is still in progress and the task remain activ clickup task ciph 24 sourc id src cu ciph 24 task id ciph 24 titl manual review threshold for low confid ocr status activ assigne diana prioriti normal date creat 2026 06 25 accept criterion quarantin folder metadata and ui indic integr end to end exercis not yet fulli done 90 confid threshold logic fulli integr with the quarantin path still in progress task remain activ clickup task ciph 24 sourc id src cu ciph 24 task id ciph 24 titl manual review threshold for low confid ocr status activ assigne diana prioriti normal date creat 2026 06 25 descript build manual review quarantin logic for low confid ocr output w 04 diana implement threshold logic a quarantin folder for low confid page and quarantin metadata confid page reason charli ad visual ui indic for quarantin page an end to end quarantin test exercis the ui and metadata path but the 90 confid threshold integr is still in progress and the task remain activ clickup task ciph 24 sourc id src cu ciph 24 task id ciph 24 titl manual review threshold for low confid ocr status activ assigne diana prioriti normal date creat 2026 06 25 activ histori 2026 06 25 diana task creat open\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e959cb748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"id\": \"33e745ef8511a565\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30029309671417637, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10114070959168055, \"vector_similarity\": 0.764982, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e959cb748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1286, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:57\", \"token_count\": 609, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-11\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Manual Review Threshold Design\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-28\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-18\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 09:08] Diana**: Starting on the manual review threshold work. We need a safety valve for when the engine isn't confident about a redaction. I'm proposing a 90% confidence threshold — anything below that gets flagged for manual review.\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 09:55] Charlie**: How do we define \\\"confidence\\\"? Just the regex match score, or are we factoring in OCR quality too?\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 10:09] Diana**: Both. If the OCR engine gives a low confidence score for a block of text, we should flag it regardless of the regex match.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 10:49] Diana**: Picking this back up — implementing the quarantine folder now. Docs that fall below the 90% threshold land there and won't be exported until a human confirms the redaction.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 13:35] Diana**: Quarantine folder alone doesn't give reviewers enough context. Designing the metadata that goes with each quarantined file: confidence score, page number, and the reason it was flagged.\\n\\n**[2026-09-05 14:34] Charlie**: Added visual indicators in the UI for quarantined pages, tied to that metadata, so reviewers can see at a glance why a page was held.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 15:55] Diana**: Ran an end-to-end pass: detection -> quarantine -> metadata -> UI markers -> manual approval. The pipeline holds together, but the 90% threshold tuning itself is still in progress — I want another round of testing before I'd call it locked.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 15:58] Charlie**: Makes sense. Let me know when you want another look at the UI side once the threshold settles.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 11 slack thread manual review threshold design channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 28 last activ 2026 09 18 2026 06 28 09 08 diana start on the manual review threshold work we need a safeti valv for when the engin isn t confid about a redact i m propos a 90 confid threshold anyth below that get flag for manual review 2026 06 28 09 55 charli how do we defin confid just the regex match score or are we factor in ocr qualiti too 2026 06 28 10 09 diana both if the ocr engin give a low confid score for a block of text we should flag it regardless of the regex match 2026 08 06 10 49 diana pick this back up implement the quarantin folder now doc that fall below the 90 threshold land there and won t be export until a human confirm the redact 2026 08 20 13 35 diana quarantin folder alon doesn t give review enough context design the metadata that go with each quarantin file confid score page number and the reason it wa flag 2026 09 05 14 34 charli ad visual indic in the ui for quarantin page tie to that metadata so review can see at a glanc whi a page wa held 2026 09 18 15 55 diana ran an end to end pas detect quarantin metadata ui marker manual approv the pipelin hold togeth but the 90 threshold tune itself is still in progress i want anoth round of test befor i d call it lock 2026 09 18 15 58 charli make sens let me know when you want anoth look at the ui side onc the threshold settl\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e917c6d48a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"id\": \"20fdff9f3b12a756\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29064818671417636, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10114070959168055, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7328323, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e917c6d48a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1695, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:51\", \"token_count\": 460, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-12\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Batch Failure Strategy (Fail-Closed)\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-12\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-07-16\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:09] Bob**: For the batch fail-closed question, we need to decide what happens if the engine crashes halfway through a 1,000-file batch. Do we keep the successful ones?\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:26] Charlie**: Absolutely not. If we can't guarantee 100% of the batch is safe, we should fail-closed. No partial exports.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:28] Bob**: Agreed. Drafting the plan now. If any worker node throws an unhandled exception, we abort the entire job and purge the output buffer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:43] Charlie**: I've added an exception hook to the core engine. It catches low-level segfaults and signals the controller to stop all active streams.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 11:23] Bob**: Implementation complete. Added an atomic rename step at the very end — the output folder stays empty until the last file is verified.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 12:53] Diana**: What about logs? We need to know *why* it failed.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:16] Bob**: Crash report gets written to a separate `audit_log.json` before the shutdown. Captures the stack trace and the filename that triggered the fault.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:17] Charlie**: Perfect. :lock:\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:19] Alice**: Thanks.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:30] Diana**: QA pass on fail-closed is done — confirmed no output file gets written on failure and the temp files get securely deleted. Signing off before the encryption and offline work start relying on this.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:31] Bob**: Calling this done.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 12 slack thread batch failur strategi fail close channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 12 last activ 2026 07 16 2026 06 12 10 09 bob for the batch fail close question we need to decid what happen if the engin crash halfway through a1 000 file batch do we keep the success one 2026 06 12 10 26 charli absolut not if we can t guarante 100 of the batch is safe we should fail close no partial export 2026 06 12 10 28 bob agre draft the plan now if ani worker node throw an unhandl except we abort the entir job and purg the output buffer 2026 06 12 10 43 charli i ve ad an except hook to the core engin it catch low level segfault and signal the control to stop all activ stream 2026 06 12 11 23 bob implement complet ad an atom renam step at the veri end the output folder stay empti until the last file is verifi 2026 06 12 12 53 diana what about log we need to know whi it fail 2026 06 12 13 16 bob crash report get written to a separ audit _ log json befor the shutdown captur the stack trace and the filenam that trigger the fault 2026 06 12 13 17 charli perfect lock 2026 06 12 13 19 alic thank 2026 07 16 09 30 diana qa pas on fail close is done confirm no output file get written on failur and the temp file get secur delet sign off befor the encrypt and offlin work start reli on this 2026 07 16 09 31 bob call this done\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e906ce748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"id\": \"1313e24c5f4d4803\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.28401821915422143, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08506245307745924, \"vector_similarity\": 0.74824834, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e906ce748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1616, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:03\", \"token_count\": 478, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- **2026-06-08**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Task opened to define fail-closed error handling for the batch engine.*\\n\\n- **2026-06-15**: Bob - Completion (Completed)\\n\\n - *Completed the fail-closed implementation.*\\n\\n- **2026-07-16**: Diana - QA validates fail-closed (no output file; secure temp deletion) (Completed)\\n\\n - *QA confirmed no output file on failure and secure temp-file deletion, ahead of encryption/offline gates depending on this behavior.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"2026 06 08 alic task creat open task open to defin fail close error handl for the batch engin 2026 06 15 bob complet complet complet the fail close implement 2026 07 16 diana qa valid fail close no output file secur temp delet complet qa confirm no output file on failur and secur temp file delet ahead of encrypt offlin gate depend on this behavior\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e961d24c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-25-Batch-Fail-Closed.md\", \"id\": \"8cc21bbe7f83191f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2547591267021763, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0450330638602519, \"vector_similarity\": 0.74411994, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-25-Batch-Fail-Closed.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e961d24c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-25-Batch-Fail-Closed.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-25-Batch-Fail-Closed.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1283, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:50\", \"token_count\": 638, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Worker Management Decision\\n\\nRetrospective note on the concurrency block confirmed 2026-08-25. For large-scale redaction jobs, the batch API moved from a synchronous blocking loop to an `asyncio`-driven queue: a single producer walks the file system and pushes document tasks, while a fixed pool of async workers pulls from the queue and orchestrates I/O against the redaction engine, built on top of the already-completed multi-threaded worker pool (T026).\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Ordering & Race Risk\\n\\nBecause documents vary widely in size, workers finish out of order. When multiple workers append to the same shared results manifest concurrently, writes can interleave and corrupt the JSON structure.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Update: Confirmed I/O Race, Throughput Regression\\n\\nConcurrency testing on 2026-08-25 confirmed the race is real, not just theoretical: under concurrent load, the race condition measurably cuts batch throughput by roughly 10% compared to the expected async speedup, because workers end up retrying/serializing around the corrupted-write recovery path. This is now blocking further rollout of the async scheduler.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Status\\n\\nT037 is **Blocked** on resolving the manifest-write race before the async scheduler can be considered production-ready; the throughput regression it causes depends directly on how the T026 worker pool's result-writing is serialized.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 worker manag decis retrospect note on the concurr block confirm 2026 08 25 for larg scale redact job the batch api move from a synchron block loop to an asyncio driven queue a singl produc walk the file system and push document task while a fix pool of async worker pull from the queue and orchestr i o against the redact engin built on top of the alreadi complet multi thread worker pool t026 sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 order race risk becaus document vari wide in size worker finish out of order when multipl worker append to the same share result manifest concurr write can interleav and corrupt the json structur sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 updat confirm i o race throughput regress concurr test on 2026 08 25 confirm the race is real not just theoret under concurr load the race condit measur cut batch throughput by rough 10 compar to the expect async speedup becaus worker end up retri serial around the corrupt write recoveri path this is now block further rollout of the async schedul sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 status t037 is block on resolv the manifest write race befor the async schedul can be consid product readi the throughput regress it caus depend direct on how the t026 worker pool s result write is serial\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9a578b28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"id\": \"188f8e49d969781d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.254530466258682, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.05003673751240282, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7316825, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9a578b28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1694, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:51\", \"token_count\": 573, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## Sign-off Basis\\n\\nSecurity sign-off on the AES-256 at-rest pipeline was withheld until the fail-closed deletion behavior for interrupted redaction runs (T015) was confirmed Completed — an unencrypted partial output left on disk after a crash would have undermined the encryption guarantee entirely. With that dependency cleared, the sign-off proceeded against the pipeline as implemented.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## What Was Reviewed\\n\\n- AES-256-GCM authenticated encryption applied to every redacted output file before it is written to its final location.\\n\\n- Key handling confined to process memory; no plaintext key material written to disk or logs.\\n\\n- Confirmed the pipeline degrades safely (refuses to write plaintext) if key material is unavailable, consistent with the fail-closed contract from T015.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## Follow-up Noted at Sign-off\\n\\nOn machines without a hardware TPM, the volume key is still derived from a user passphrase via PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 at 100k iterations. This is not a blocker for the AES-256 pipeline sign-off itself, but Diana flagged it as a hardening follow-up: moving to Argon2id would meaningfully raise the cost of offline brute-force against weak passphrases on non-TPM hardware.\\n\\n*Status*: AES-256 at-rest pipeline signed off as Completed. Passphrase-derived key hardening (Argon2id) tracked separately as a pre-v1.0 hardening item, not a sign-off condition.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 sign off basi secur sign off on the ae 256 at rest pipelin wa withheld until the fail close delet behavior for interrupt redact run t015 wa confirm complet an unencrypt partial output left on disk after a crash would have undermin the encrypt guarante entir with that depend clear the sign off proceed against the pipelin a implement sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 what wa review ae 256 gcm authent encrypt appli to everi redact output file befor it is written to it final locat key handl confin to process memori no plaintext key materi written to disk or log confirm the pipelin degrad safe refus to write plaintext if key materi is unavail consist with the fail close contract from t015 sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 follow up note at sign off on machin without a hardwar tpm the volum key is still deriv from a user passphras via pbkdf2 hmac sha256 at 100k iter this is not a blocker for the ae 256 pipelin sign off itself but diana flag it a a harden follow up move to argon2id would meaning rais the cost of offlin brute forc against weak passphras on non tpm hardwar status ae 256 at rest pipelin sign off a complet passphras deriv key harden argon2id track separ a a pre v1 0 harden item not a sign off condit\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e99eb05e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"id\": \"3d30fbd4bb571642\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.25437772715422147, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08506245307745924, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6494467, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e99eb05e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1518, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:57\", \"token_count\": 466, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-25\\n\\