", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-06-28-OCR-Pipeline-Design.md\", \"id\": \"07db511d3baaa380\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.25251380625868197, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.05003673751240282, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7249603, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-06-28-OCR-Pipeline-Design.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9b3d77c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-06-28-OCR-Pipeline-Design.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-06-28-OCR-Pipeline-Design.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 783, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:37\", \"token_count\": 427, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-03\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: OCR Progress Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-07-05\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nCharlie reported the Tesseract OCR fallback is usable but still serial-and-slow on large docs. No redesign this meeting; parallelization deferred until the bottleneck is clearer.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-03\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: OCR Progress Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-07-05\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Charlie**: OCR POC update — Tesseract is wired for pages that fail the text-layer path. On large documents it's still slow because we're going page by page in series.\\n\\n**Bob**: Is that good enough to leave in progress, or do we need a redesign now?\\n\\n**Charlie**: Leave it in progress. The POC proves the fallback path. Performance tuning can come once w